## 4. What to check for each section, and where

Treat the "Where to look" column as categories and fill in the actual files of the repo being documented.

| Section | What to check | Where to look |
|---|---|---|
| repo / Owner | repo URL; Owner ({{#if has.owner_source}}from {{ scope.owner_source }}{{else}}the user's call{{/if}}; `unknown` when not known) | `git remote -v` |
| What it does | purpose, role, **capabilities** (endpoints / grants / features), each deployment's responsibility | README; for a frontend, the route or page table |
| Architecture | **runtime version** (recorded only here), framework type, layering, patterns | dependency manifests, startup / registration entry points |
| Dependencies | upstreams **grouped by domain**, RPC / SDK usage, HTTP timeouts; Consumed by | runtime config files, client registration |
| Environments | which environments actually exist + the platform of each; Domains/ingress (including wildcard aliases), the deploy-unit details; the public host per env | deploy manifests, CI config, per-env config transforms, container build file{{#if has.external_reference}}; the per-env host list in the external reference ({{ derived.labels.external_reference }}){{/if}} |
| Health/probes · Scaling | liveness / readiness paths; autoscaling min / max / threshold + resource requests / limits | deploy manifests, health-check mapping (separate inbound probes from internal monitors) |
| Data stores | the DBs (**verify the engine**), secret source | runtime config, data-access registration |
| Cache store | the shared cache or key-value store and what it holds | runtime config, cache client registration |
{{#each capabilities.shared_catalogs}}
| {{ this.source_field }} | the {{ this.name }} each env uses, or `none`; mechanism in parentheses | registration code; the matching monitoring manifest when config holds only a secret or template; the full roll-up is `platform-basics.md` |
{{/each}}
| Caching / Retry | cache layers + TTL; retry, backoff, circuit breaker, timeout, rate limit | registration code, resilience-policy files, config |
| Background jobs | scheduler + storage + dashboard, schedule list; none = `none` | scheduler registration, job classes |
| Security | inbound auth / token validation, rate limit, CSRF / CORS, signing (only if present) | startup, middleware, request filters, authorization attributes |
{{#if has.global_settings}}
| Settings | the namespace + how it is loaded | {{ capabilities.global_settings.lookup }} (§5) + the loading code |
{{/if}}
| Assets / i18n | translation tooling; asset front-record{{#if has.external_reference}} (the authoritative list lives in the external reference, **not** in code){{/if}} | dependency manifests |
| Dev & testing | how to run / mock; **Unit / Integration / E2E listed separately** (runtime version is under Architecture) | README, test projects, CI config |
{{#if has.observability_doc}}
