{{/if}}

**Use an Explore agent for one sweep.** Prompt skeleton:

```
Explore {{ paths.repos_root }}/<repo>. I am writing a structured knowledge doc and need decision-grade facts with file:line; say "not found" rather than guessing.
Read the README / dependency manifests / runtime config (including per-env variants) / startup and registration code / container build file /
deploy manifests (ingress, autoscaling, probes) / CI config (look at how many environments actually exist), and report:
1 repo URL  2 purpose / role + capabilities  3 architecture (version / framework / layering / patterns)
4 ingress hosts + wildcards + the public host per env  5 namespace / container port / image (if containerized)
6 health / probe endpoints (separate inbound probes from internal monitors)  7 scaling (autoscaling + resource requests / limits)
8 upstreams (grouped by domain) + timeouts  9 consumed by  10 data stores and the cache store, if any (verify the DB engine from the data-access setup; REDACT secrets)
{{#if has.shared_catalogs}}11 each shared-catalog field (see §3)  {{/if}}{{#if has.global_settings}}12 settings namespace  {{/if}}13 caching + TTL
14 retry / resilience  15 background jobs (scheduler + schedule list; none = none)
16 security (auth / token validation / rate limit / CSRF / CORS — only if present)  17 metrics endpoint (do not be fooled by substrings)
18 CI/CD + platform + deployment  19 testing (unit / integration / E2E separately)  20 logging (library → sink + the configured identity)
Give file:line for each item, copy original values, redact every secret; verify the nature of health / metrics / DB engine, do not be fooled by strings.
```

